    {
      "page_title": "Design Rules & Last Traps",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Design Guidance"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Make each manager do exactly one thing",
            "Keep __exit__ non-throwing and idempotent",
            "Never suppress by default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Not Just For Files",
          "text": "`with` is Python's general mechanism for guaranteeing a paired action completes. Any set/restore, begin/commit or enter/leave belongs inside one."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "cm = mgr()",
            "with cm: pass",
            "with cm: pass   # RuntimeError:",
            "                # generator didn't yield"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Partial Setup Leaks",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "__enter__ grabs #1, then raises grabbing #2",
            "__exit__ never runs, so #1 leaks",
            "Fix: hold an internal ExitStack inside __enter__",
            "pop_all() only once every acquire succeeded"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Wrong Beliefs"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`with suppress(Exception):` over a big block hides failures",
            "And silently skips the rest of the block",
            "`with` does NOT swallow exceptions — it guarantees cleanup",
            "Holding a lock for a whole function hurts concurrency"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Last Three Traps",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "sqlite3 conn as manager commits, never closes",
            "Wrap it: `with closing(connect(db)) as c:` too",
            "`with` on async manager, `async with` on sync — both TypeError",
            "Deep nesting = right-drift with zero added safety"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "with closing(sqlite3.connect(db)) as c:",
            "    with c:              # commits/rolls back",
            "        c.execute(sql)   # outer also closes"
          ]
        },
        {
