        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Async Rules Worth Keeping",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`async with` outside `async def` is a SyntaxError",
            "__aexit__ can await — sync __exit__ cannot",
            "CancelledError reaches __aexit__ like any exception",
            "Shield or `finally` if teardown must complete",
            "`async with` takes the comma form too"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "@asynccontextmanager",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@asynccontextmanager",
            "async def conn(url):",
            "    c = await connect(url)",
            "    try:",
            "        yield c",
            "    finally:",
            "        await c.close()"
          ],
          "note": "exactly one yield, like the sync form"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "asyncio Managers"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`async with lock:` — ==asyncio.Lock==",
            "`asyncio.Semaphore` caps concurrent coroutines",
            "`TaskGroup` awaits **all** children on exit",
            "`ClientSession()` closes its connection pool"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async with AsyncExitStack() as s:",
            "    sess = await s.enter_async_context(",
            "        ClientSession())",
            "    s.push_async_callback(flush)"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
